# References and rename of a local and of a `match` arm binding inside bodies
# deferred to their calls (`comptime` parameters) follow the syntactic scope
# that declares them
# (issues/fixed/2026-10-24-lsp-references-of-a-parameter-match-every-same-named-parameter-of-the-module.md).
# `h` and `k` each bind a local `y`, and `k`'s `match` arm binds another `y`.
# The deferred bodies' atoms carry no ExprInfo, and every `y` of the module
# used to be one symbol: references on `h`'s `y` and on `k`'s arm `y`
# returned all six, and renaming `k`'s local renamed `h`'s too. Now each
# answers its own declaration's occurrences.
timeout=240
framing=strict
